-- Index and type of operators on the integral columns at a p-adic place
-- (IndexDvd, HasType), marked sets of primes of E above p, the scaled
-- Hecke operator p^{A_l} T_{l,𝔯} at a marked prime, and the chain of lifts
-- B_μ with good data, read from the rest of layer 5.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Columns/TwistedHeckeType.lean ("A
-- Frobenius-twisted Hecke operator has small elementary divisors. ...
-- Trading denominators at the level prime for a column operator."), with
-- New/Core/ModuleIndex.lean (IndexDvd, HasType),
-- New/Exchange/CrudeModularData.lean (Data.inducedPlace, Data.IsMarked,
-- Data.IsFullMark, Data.markExponent, Data.evenPlaces, Data.Bμ,
-- Data.lowColumns), New/Columns/JetExponentBound.lean
-- (Data.IsMarked.markOperator), New/Columns/ChainValuation.lean
-- (IsGoodDatum).
-- Encoding. The O_ι-modules are subsets of the columns closed under sums
-- and O_ι-multiples, O_ι = embValRing(p, ι) as a subring of ℂ; a square
-- matrix over O_ι is indexed by a natural number k. The marked prime l
-- is a finite place of E; the source's subtype Λ is a set of places. The
-- forms on Y_m that B_μ produces are read with the weight datum and rank
-- of the level setting liftLevelSetting(P, D, L, ϑ). FORWARD (placeholder
-- bodies): the split Hecke operator T_{l,i} (heckeSplit of
-- Lib/Weil/Unramified/SphericalHecke.lean), the chain B_μ = restrictToY ∘
-- chainComb (CrudeModularData.lean, Data.Bμ: the chains of lift kernels of
-- New/Seesaw and New/Rows), and IsGoodDatum (ChainValuation.lean: the
-- admissible translations and the joint invariance of New/Seesaw). Not
-- stated here: this file's own lemmas (norm_detCharAt_diagN_le,
-- name_lastColDatum_mem_raises, chain₂_pairTranslates_eq_smul_chain,
-- gaugeLe_Bmu_at_N, Columns.hasType_markOperator), which need the
-- twisting data, the Fourier operators at N and the Hecke size bounds of
-- New/TwistedHecke.
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
